Track 3: Tape-Saturated Ecdysis
- Story & Context: When the morning cleaning crew entered the abandoned terminus at Kayes Station, they found Carriage 12 completely empty yet resonating with an unearthly, soaring polyrhythm that tasted like cold tea and rust on the tongue. Hung from an emergency brake valve, an unattended pocket synthesizer was endlessly recycling an airborne highlife guitar loop through a battery-powered tape delay, locked into the hollow shake of a abandoned dried gourd rocking with the wind. The stationmaster refused to shut it off for three days, swearing he could hear the ghost of a thousand travelers chanting the final refrain: "leave the empty shell upon the luggage rack."
